    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0657" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/172a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-06T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>104. For General Russell.</p>
                <p>Has Haitian Government formally appointed members of Claims Commission? If not,
                    urge immediate action upon nomination of Mr. Stanley<anchor n="95"
                        xml:id="d463-f1"/> and upon nominations by Financial Adviser as sent to
                    President Borno in Financial Adviser’s letter of September 22.<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d463-f2"/></p>
                <p>Department believes President Borno should inform Financial Adviser by letter
                    that persons referred to have been appointed to serve on Claims Commission in
                    accordance with terms of protocol, specifying in case of European members that
                    they are to serve only while claims of their nationals are under consideration.
                    Financial Adviser should then formally notify appointee either direct or through
                    Department.</p>
                <pb facs="0658" n="544" xml:id="pg544"/>
                <p>Also urge immediate appointment of Haitian member. It is necessary that
                    appointees be formally notified at once, as Mr. Stanley will sail November
                    15th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d463-f1" n="95" xml:id="d463-f1-content">
                <p>John S. Stanley, nominated by the Secretary of State as American member.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d463-f2" n="96" xml:id="d463-f2-content">
